"Precision Touchpad" = "Precision Touchpad";
"Precision Touchpad Hint" = "Send the trackpad's multi-finger touches to a Windows 11 host as a precision touchpad, so Windows handles scrolling, pinch and three- or four-finger gestures itself. Block mode sends every finger to Windows and stops the Mac from also moving, clicking or scrolling with the same fingers. Use-both mode keeps a single finger on the normal Mac pointer and clicks; as soon as a second finger lands, the whole gesture goes to Windows until all fingers lift. In Block mode Windows moves its own pointer and this Mac cannot tell where it is, so opening the floating control ball with the pointer and sliding onto another display will not line up with the cursor you see; choose Use-both if you rely on those. Needs a Windows 11 host that supports it; otherwise normal mouse input is used.";
