"Optional" = "Optional";
"Accessibility" = "Accessibility";
"Welcome Accessibility detail" = "Optional. Lets Moonlight send macOS shortcuts such as ⌘Tab and ⌘Space to the host, and keep trackpad gestures from acting on this Mac while the precision touchpad is on.";
"Capture System Shortcuts Hint" = "While the stream has the mouse and keyboard, shortcuts macOS normally keeps for itself (⌘Tab, ⌘`, ⌘Space, ⌃Space, ⌃ arrow keys, screenshots, function keys) are sent to the host instead. ⌘ is the Win key unless the keyboard translation says otherwise, so ⌘Tab opens Task View. Force Quit (⌥⌘Esc) and Lock Screen (⌃⌘Q) always stay with macOS. Release the mouse to use your Mac's shortcuts again. Warning: Mac shortcuts such as ⌘Q are then sent to the host too, so ⌘Q will not quit Moonlight; use the stream's disconnect or quit shortcut.";
"Capture System Shortcuts Permission Hint" = "Accessibility access is not granted, so macOS still handles its own shortcuts such as ⌘Tab while streaming. Grant Moonlight access under Privacy & Security > Accessibility.";
"Capture System Shortcuts Permission Title" = "Allow Moonlight to capture system shortcuts?";
"Capture System Shortcuts Permission Message" = "To send shortcuts such as ⌘Tab and ⌘Space to the host, macOS requires Accessibility access for Moonlight. You can grant it now or later in System Settings > Privacy & Security > Accessibility. Without it, macOS keeps handling those shortcuts.";
"Grant Access" = "Grant Access";
"Grant Accessibility Access" = "Grant Access";
"Translation Rules Capture Warning" = "To record a macOS system shortcut such as ⌘Tab or ⌘Space as a trigger, turn on Capture System Shortcuts first. Warning: while capture is on and the stream has the keyboard, Mac shortcuts such as ⌘Q are sent to the host and will not act on this Mac (for example, ⌘Q will not quit Moonlight). Use the stream's disconnect or quit shortcut instead; if needed, Force Quit (⌥⌘Esc) still works because it is never captured.";
"Translation Rule System Shortcut Warning" = "This is a macOS system shortcut. The rule only works while Capture System Shortcuts is on and has Accessibility access; otherwise macOS may act on it as well, or the rule may not fire at all.";
"Shortcut needs system shortcut capture" = "This is a macOS system shortcut. Turn on Capture System Shortcuts to record and use it as a trigger.";
"Shortcut never captured" = "Force Quit (⌥⌘Esc) and Lock Screen (⌃⌘Q) always stay with macOS and can't be used as triggers.";
"Translation Rule Needs Capture" = "This trigger is a macOS system shortcut and only works while Capture System Shortcuts is on.";
"Precision Touchpad Gesture Permission Title" = "Block macOS gestures while streaming?";
"Precision Touchpad Gesture Permission Message" = "Moonlight can keep three- and four-finger macOS gestures, such as Mission Control and swiping between Spaces, from also acting on this Mac while the trackpad is sent to Windows. This needs Accessibility access. Without it the precision touchpad still works, but those gestures also trigger on the Mac.";
